# ── Local Firebase project override ─────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in to point THIS machine's dev
# server at a scratch Firebase project instead of the live tournament.
#
# Why you want this: AdminView auto-saves to Firestore on edit, so a dev server
# aimed at production can corrupt a real round with one stray click. With two
# developers, assume it will happen eventually.
#
# Leave every line below unset (or delete .env.local) to use production —
# that's the default and what Vercel builds use.
#
# Values come from the Firebase console: Project settings → General → Your apps
# → SDK setup and configuration. Create a fresh project (e.g. "bourbon-cup-dev"),
# add a Web app, then deploy the shared rules to it:
#
#   firebase use <your-dev-project-id> && firebase deploy --only firestore:rules
#
# All six are required together; setting only some throws at startup.

# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
# VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ── Serverless API secrets (api/*.js) ───────────────────────────────
# Only needed if you run `vercel dev` and exercise the GHIN / course lookups.
# In production these are set in the Vercel project, not here. Get the values
# from Aaron via a password manager — never commit them.

# GHIN_EMAIL=
# GHIN_PASSWORD=
# GHIN_COUNTRY=USA
# GOLF_COURSE_API_KEY=
# RAPIDAPI_KEY=
